---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_URL } from '../lib/site.mjs'

const description = `The privacy policy for ${SITE_NAME}: what data is collected, the cookies advertising partners set, how Google uses them, and how to turn personalised ads off.`
const EMAIL = 'hello@gta6record.com'
const UPDATED = '15 September 2026'
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" description={description} path="/privacy" updated={UPDATED}>
  <section class="band band--glaze">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="crumb" style="color:var(--on-glaze-2)"><a href="/" style="color:var(--on-glaze-2)">GTA 6 Record</a> / Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Last updated {UPDATED}. This policy covers {SITE_URL}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="shell prose">

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This site does not ask you for your name, your email address, or any account.
    There is no login and no newsletter. The only personal data that reaches the
    site is what your browser sends automatically, plus whatever our advertising
    partners collect through cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>What is collected</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Server records.</strong> Our host records ordinary request data such
      as your IP address, the page asked for, the time, and your browser type.
      This is used to keep the site running and to spot abuse.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Advertising data.</strong> Third party advertising partners may set
      cookies and read device identifiers. This is explained below.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Email you send us.</strong> If you email us, we keep the message so
      we can reply. Nothing more is done with it.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal data. We do not build profiles of readers ourselves.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    A cookie is a small file a website stores in your browser. This site sets no
    cookies of its own. Cookies you may still receive here come from our
    advertising partners.
  </p>

  <h2>Google and advertising</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Third party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve adverts based on your earlier visits to this and other websites.</li>
    <li>
      Google's use of advertising cookies lets it and its partners serve adverts to
      you based on your visits to this and other sites. You can turn personalised
      advertising off in
      <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can opt out of personalised advertising from many other vendors at
      <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Google's own policy is at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">policies.google.com</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Shopping links</h2>
  <p>
    Some pages contain links to shops, including the Amazon Associates programme.
    If you buy something after following one of those links, this site may earn a
    commission. It costs you nothing extra. Those shops set their own cookies to
    track the referral, and their own privacy policies apply once you leave here.
  </p>
  <p>
    A paid link never changes what is written on a page. Facts are not upgraded
    because a link next to them pays.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Block or delete cookies in your browser settings at any time. The site still works.</li>
    <li>Use the opt-out links above to stop personalised advertising.</li>
    <li>Email us to ask what we hold about you, or to ask us to delete an email you sent.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>If you are in the EU, the UK, or California</h2>
  <p>
    You have rights over your personal data, including the right to see it, to
    correct it, to have it deleted, and to object to it being used for
    advertising. To use any of those rights, email
    <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. We answer within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is not aimed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect
    data from them. If you believe a child has sent us personal data, email us and
    it will be deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Every page here links out to its sources. Once you follow a link, you are on
    someone else's site and their privacy policy applies, not this one.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it. Material changes
    will be noted on this page rather than made quietly.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions go to <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. General
    questions go through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
